//.vmt file generated by MAYA. Remove this line if you edit this file! -- theo 
//
// SiN VR -- hands hidden. Restore hands.vmt.sinvr-original to get them back.
//
// Confirmed by deleting this file: the hand went pink/black checker while the
// gun stayed normal. This material IS read, and it IS the hand.
//
// Why "$alpha" 0 never worked, three attempts running:
//
//     hands.vtf   1024x1024  flags=0x01000000   <- NO alpha channel at all
//
// $translucent enables alpha BLENDING; blending needs alpha to come from
// somewhere, and the $alpha material constant does not reach this path. With no
// alpha in the texture the result is opaque no matter what the material says.
//
// Tools/toolsinvisible was the next mistake: it HAS 8-bit alpha, but it is
// Hammer's editor texture -- semi-transparent MAGENTA, meant to be seen in the
// editor. "Invisible" there describes the brush, not the texture.
//
// hands_hidden.vtf is built from toolsinvisible's header (a VTF the engine
// already loads: 7.1, DXT5, 64x64, alpha flag set) with every pixel byte zeroed.
// In DXT5 an all-zero alpha block means both endpoints are 0 and every index
// selects endpoint 0, so alpha is 0 for every texel -- genuinely transparent.
"VertexLitGeneric"
{
	"$basetexture"	"models/weapons/v_hands/hands_hidden"
	"$model"		1
	"$translucent"	1
}
